  * ComfyUI_LayerStyle (layer effects port)
      Author:   chflame163
      Source:   https://github.com/chflame163/ComfyUI_LayerStyle
      License:  MIT (declared in the upstream pyproject.toml and README;
                the clone under third_party/ ships no LICENSE file).
      Usage:    nodes/layer_effects/ is a PORT, not a clean-room rewrite.
                The eight MEC/LayerEffects nodes carry the feature union of
                upstream's V1/V2/V3 variants of drop_shadow, inner_shadow,
                outer_glow, inner_glow, stroke, color_overlay,
                gradient_overlay and gradient_map.

                Reimplemented in torch rather than copied verbatim, for a
                concrete reason: upstream's py/blendmodes.py imports the
                `blend_modes` pip package, which is not installed in this
                ComfyUI, so a straight copy would fail at import. The blend
                table is checked against a numpy transcription of the
                upstream formulas in tests/test_layer_effects.py.

                Four defects in the upstream are fixed here and each has a
                test: an UnboundLocalError at zero offset, a size-mismatched
                mask being replaced with solid white, a python list returned
                through an IMAGE socket, and RGBA returned on an IMAGE socket.
                The sign of distance_x/distance_y is deliberately inverted
                relative to upstream so that positive moves the shadow right.

                The front-end (js/c2c_layer_effects.js) is original work: the
                upstream ships none for these nodes.

                Second batch, nodes/mask_toolkit/: the LayerMask family. Only
                the five capabilities this pack did not already have were
                ported - Mask From Color, Mask Gradient, Mask Grain, Mask
                Motion Blur and Edge Spread - plus a channel selector and
                Blend-If soft ends folded into the EXISTING LuminanceKeyerMEC
                rather than added as a sixth node. The rest of LayerMask was
                deliberately not ported: MaskEdgeUltraDetail V1/V2/V3,
                MaskGrow, MaskEdgeShrink, MaskInvert and MaskPreview are
                covered by MaskRefineMEC, MaskStroke by LayerEffectStrokeMEC,
                MaskBoxDetect/Extend by nodes/bbox_nodes.py, and the eight
                Segformer nodes and RemBgUltra need model weights.
                Front-ends in js/c2c_mask_toolkit.js and the shared
                js/_c2c_fx_controls.js are original work.

